id: pm-ado-sdk-history-fence
title: Adopt decision-bound native revision guards for Azure lifecycle writes
description: "Own the #47 adoption slice for SDK withExpectedItemRevisions: bind each native lifecycle dispatch to the saved canonical decision document, preserve monotonic pre/post history detection and forward-only recovery, and retain explicit older-host compatibility. Remaining locked monotonic-history and storage-override conformance acceptance is split into pm-ado-monotonic-write-guard; backend authority/recovery and filesystem/database conformance are separate Feature children of the roadmap owner. Earlier diagnostic failures and decisions remain in append-only history."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[5]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1576","gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1620",sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli#1576","upstream:pm-cli#1620"
created_at: "2026-10-27T13:44:23.397Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T18:58:46.958Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-ado-sdk-adoption
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T16:36:12.343Z",codex-agent,"R7 audit links the already-open upstream issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1576. Installed SDK 2026.10.24 BulkItemUpdateMutation.match accepts only a metadata key/value; BulkItemCloseMutation has no match or expectedItemHash/expectedHistoryHead. commitWorkspaceTransaction provides a workspace lease but ordinary native writers acquire item leases independently. mutateItemWithHistoryContext permits history reads inside its callback, but cannot compose a native lifecycle update under that same non-reentrant item lease. The internal runWithItemMutationPrecondition callback is synchronous and not a public SDK export. A beforeMutation hook can inspect history under the native item lease; SDK setActiveExtensionHooks replaces the full registry and offers no public additive scoped guard or registry snapshot. Disabling extensions as in a hook workaround would bypass existing policy/hooks and lose extension-owned runtime schema; hand-applying native update/close/hierarchy behavior would violate SDK adoption. Required public contract: native lifecycle/bulk expectedHistoryHead (length plus record hash), or expectedItemHash, checked under the existing item lease; alternatively an additive request-scoped transactional guard that preserves the active extension runtime. Native sync update sites and resolution agreement publication remain blocked on this contract; not marked fixed. A package-level fixed-clock boundary probe is being captured in disposable source copies with the real SDK."
  "2026-10-27T17:08:11.670Z",codex-agent,"R7 capability check also inspected the public SDK 2026.10.27 declarations from a credential-free npm pack without changing the pin. No native expected item/hash/history-head precondition was exported there either. RelationshipEventStore.expectedVersion guards its separate relationship ledger, not native item parent/dependency/lifecycle writes. Additional SDK facade audit: index.ts importRelations forward updates and compensation also call an opaque PmClient.update without a history precondition; that facade cannot enforce a native item CAS with its current client contract. These sites join sync commitLocal and resolution publication under upstream #1576. The fixed-clock probe fails all 18 cases: history advances in all 18; 15 return incorrect success; 6 overwrite the peer title; all 18 change item state after the peer edit. Revert proof is not applicable to an unimplemented SDK contract; the finding remains unresolved, not marked fixed."
  "2026-10-27T20:28:55.116Z",codex-agent,"R8 implements the owner-approved package fallback for upstream pm-cli#1576: native history length/hash before inspection; SDK lifecycle write inside a workspace transaction; locked post-write native author/op/patch verification; selective append-only compensation and typed conflict if another entry intervened. Journal keys bind the head, and unverified dispatch/verified-but-uncommitted journals resume without redispatch. The missing native pre-write API remains an upstream follow-up, rather than an unmet package acceptance criterion. Existing SDK hooks and runtime remain active; native clients and sync adapters share history-fence.ts."
  "2026-10-28T18:52:09.354Z",codex-agent,"Escalated review critical-section prerequisite is not provided by pinned SDK 2026.10.25. Broad commitWorkspaceTransaction holds sdk-workspace-transaction, but native sdk.update and PmClient.update do not acquire that lock. A second OS process commits title, parent, relation and assignee edits between locked inspect and apply; the later write loses each peer edit and the coordinator returns committed in all four cases. Reproduced with published 2026.10.28 too. Needed SDK contract: every native lifecycle writer joins a reentrant workspace transaction lease, or expectedItemHash/history-head precondition checked under the native item lock (upstream unbraind/pm-cli#1576). No upstream repository changes or issue filed. Existing issue enriched rather than duplicate creation."
  "2026-10-28T18:55:50.755Z",codex-agent,"Final linked diagnostic run: four cases, four isolation violations, command exit 4 (pm test reports one failed linked command). Pinned dependency unchanged. npm run build:test and npm run typecheck pass; npm run docstring passes 19 files / 115 declarations. No lint script exists. The diagnostic is deliberately not a release acceptance test and its failure is a blocker, not an expected success. No product fix or behavioral revert proof is claimed."
  "2026-10-28T21:36:48.211Z",codex-agent,"Owner confirmed ordinary-writer isolation gap as unbraind/pm-cli#1620 beside #1576 and authorized a forward-only policy. Removed native compensation and abandoned-journal replay; local snapshots/history are detection only, never restore authority. SDK hierarchy validation handles forward parent changes. Added X/A/B cycle fixture and close-intent peer fixture; both preserve durable forward state and peer edits with typed sync_conflict. Known final-read/write window will be measured and documented rather than claimed closed."
  "2026-10-28T21:51:42.828Z",codex-agent,"Forward-only native guard suite: 52/52 pass with 100% lines/branches/functions. No reverse mutation exists. Structured prewrite receipts cover sets, explicit clears, absent targets, legacy streams, default creator receipts and fixed-clock ABA. The measured final-guard-to-SDK-completion sample is 34.8–194.7 ms for 12 writes on the shared host (upper bound, not an isolation guarantee or maximum). Native compensation behavioral revert fails both review-derived fixtures; old intent-proof refusal revert fails retry fixture."
  "2026-10-28T23:12:07.930Z",codex-agent,"The supported interim policy is forward-only rather than an atomic isolation claim. SDK #1576 lacks native expected-history CAS; #1620 confirms commitWorkspaceTransaction does not serialize ordinary writers. Every remaining native write re-reads current fields/history, reports observed changes as sync_conflict, and never restores old pm values. Twelve real SDK samples bounded final guard through completed write at 34.8-194.7 ms; scheduling and hooks can lengthen that window. Reviewer cycle and old compensation-intent fixtures plus every crash/peer boundary are acceptance tests. The independent workspace capability probe remains a failing diagnostic, not a passing safety claim."
  "2026-10-28T23:13:02.089Z",codex-agent,"Revert evidence: disposable rebuilt copies with compensation re-enabled fail both reviewer safety fixtures (2 failures, stale parent and obsolete intent restored). Adding the previous intent-history proof refusal alone fails its recovery fixture (1 failure). Production has no restore/compensation mutation path; retained native history is read-only evidence. Every old event remains append-only and readable; no repair is required to resume."
  "2026-10-28T23:19:40.701Z",codex-agent,"Final integration acceptance passes 115/115, including 100 boundary crash/second-process edit cases, six native dispatch crash cases and reviewer recovery fixtures. No peer domain value is rolled back, no parent cycle or duplicate remote object is introduced, and retries either proceed or report normal sync_conflict rather than demand intent repair. Final-source revert controls pass 3/3 after disposable reverts (compensation2 and proof-refusal1 failures). Native helper focused suite remains 52/52 with 100% lines/branches/functions. Remaining last-read/native-write isolation limitation is deliberately documented, not hidden by expected failures."
  "2026-10-29T00:28:20.869Z",codex-agent,"Additional coverage guards exercise both missing and partial endpoint bases, peer parent clears, native policy refusal, explicit resolution retiring old checkpoints, and export immediately after an interrupted native close. These preserve existing domain/HTTP/history invariants; only the owner-required obsolete-intent discard suffix is allowed. The completed V8 run retained all SDK hierarchy/ownership tests and the 500-outcome/512-two-sided models; source coverage was 100% lines/functions and 99.74% branches before these additions, so no full-gate pass was claimed."
  "2026-10-29T00:32:01.991Z",codex-agent,"Final controls: linked native52/52 and expanded integration121/121, source/build relation peer-assign/clear/delete coverage, actual SDK policy-hook refusal, resolution checkpoint retirement and export-first close recovery. Final behavioral reverts: compensation2 failures and old proof-refusal1 failure; fixed reviewer controls pass. The current source still has no compensation path; all source changes this round net -80 lines across history-fence.ts, index.ts and sync.ts. Awaiting strict full npm/Bun gates, without claiming atomic isolation."
  "2026-10-29T01:35:39.439Z",codex-agent,"The final source preserves all native SDK PmCliError exit codes, including usage2 and conflict4; source and built real-hook/ownership controls pass8/8. This removes local SDK error reclassification without changing any timestamp/history/compensation policy. The completed local934-test run passed every test but failed the strict branch gate before this cleanup; do not treat it as full-gate approval. Full npm and Bun release jobs remain required in PR CI, with the owner45-minute post-push wait limit."
  "2026-10-29T01:49:39.126Z",codex-agent,"Shipping forward-only policy is documented in README Concurrency: no rollback can overwrite a peer or create the reviewer parent cycle; stale mutable intents are discarded with a recognized native reason and never demand proof repair. Own native history is read-only progress evidence, not permission to restore fields. Reviewer reverts still fail2+1 and fixed controls3/3 pass; native52/52 and integration123/123 plus SDK refusal8/8/native precondition19/19 pass. Native expected-history CAS remains upstream#1576 and workspace-vs-ordinary-writer isolation upstream#1620. Measured final-read/completed-write bound34.8-194.7ms is a sample, not isolation or a guaranteed maximum. Full npm/Bun CI remains required at all four100% thresholds; release claim without closing this upstream-gap item."
  "2026-10-29T02:01:42.320Z",codex-agent,"Implementation commit f58483ae58d9cf9e8f815f2381d25773452655f3 is pushed in PR46: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/46 . Implementation round net -422 lines (1602 added/2024 deleted), production native fence/relation import/sync net -80 (235 added/315 deleted). Source CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40803317217 currently has 0 passed/4 running (Node22,Node26,npm release,Bun release); CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40803317026 passed1/1. Full release evidence is pending, not approval. This final metadata receipt requires fresh exact-head CI; the original45-minute wait cutoff remains2026-10-29 02:40 UTC and is not reset by the receipt push. Claims remain released and neither item is closed."
  "2026-10-29T02:21:54.690Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the interim SDK-exit-code note: native conflict4 remains a sync conflict, other SDK validation failures retain the prior ADO_REMOTE/provider-failure3 receipt. The transient all-exit-code propagation was reverted to preserve user-visible behavior. Real source/built ownership fixtures now use an already-agreed assignee so they actually reach the SDK writer policy; all synced fields and native bytes remain unchanged on refusal. Focused7/7 exercise both line459 branches, and the prior empty-title validation expectation remains intact. The concurrency policy is unchanged: no automatic compensation, no intent-proof repair, with #1576/#1620 explicitly documented."
  "2026-10-29T03:13:45.306Z",codex-agent,"Final no-overwrite sweep removes the mode exception from indirect relation guards: import, export recovery and sync all compare current endpoints with their agreed base. Known endpoint conflicts stop dependent provider calls; current fields survive retries. Cold scalar bases use the same three-way decision rather than implicit import authority. Source/built legacy and partial-base tests preserve peer edits, and explicit resolution still works. Real SDK policy fixtures distinguish merge refusal from writer policy; original SDK conflict4/provider-validation3 receipts are preserved. Regression34/34 and new controls12/12 pass. Behavioral reverts fail4 endpoint-mode scenarios plus4 cold-base scenarios; fixed12/12 pass, alongside the prior compensation2/proof1 failures. #1576/#1620 and the measured SDK read/write window remain documented. No automatic rollback or history repair exists. CI on the final push remains pending at the already elapsed original cutoff."
  "2026-11-06T17:33:02.621Z",codex-astra,"Adoption resumed for #47. Public SDK exports withExpectedItemRevisions(expectations, operation, context) and canonical document hashing allow a locked write precondition without replacing native lifecycle policy/hooks. Preserve append-only history checks separately: content CAS alone does not prevent ABA. First add a deterministic separate-process peer-write regression and demonstrate failure on main. Older hosts retain their documented detection-only compatibility; no silent claim of guarded writes."
  "2026-11-06T17:38:50.636Z",codex-astra,"Baseline reproduction on main 0b3d5a3: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"decision-bound revision guards\" test/history-fence.test.ts fails all 12 source/built field cases (13 failures including parent test). Each separate OS-process peer commits after final package reads; the old dispatcher then changes the peer document before reporting sync_conflict. New implementation wraps the existing dispatcher in withExpectedItemRevisions using hashDocument(saved decision document), retaining native history checks and forward-only policy. Added unchecked-dispatch and unjournalled legacy-document controls; full targeted verification pending."
  "2026-11-06T17:48:48.196Z",codex-astra,"Existing owner narrowed to the delivered revision-guard adoption, not duplicated. The open Feature pm-ado-monotonic-write-guard owns the remaining monotonic audit-coordinate and post-PR1658 storage-override acceptance; pm-ado-backend-contract and pm-ado-backend-conformance own the other roadmap slices. No item is closed in this session."
  "2026-11-06T17:50:45.401Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable rebuilt source copy: restoring only NativeWriteFence.update to main behavior makes every new regression scenario fail (23/23 reported tests including three parent tests). Replacing only the saved decision hash with a later readItemRevision makes both pre-dispatch decision-binding cases fail (3/7 reported failures including parent; four controls pass). Restored implementation rebuilt and passes all 23/23, no skips. Command: node --test --test-reporter=spec --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"decision-bound revision guards\" test/history-fence.test.ts; late-read mutant uses pattern \"decision-bound revision guards refuse unjournalled\". Original checkout never reverted. The passing corpus includes 12 separate-process field interleavings, two owned-write scope-advancement cases, unjournalled legacy document edits, decision binding and unchecked dispatch."
  "2026-11-06T18:08:07.511Z",codex-astra,"Bounded #47 adoption is implemented in PR92, implementation commit 9a6665e15f387d03ba81a4d772181e45688a8d1c. Native fixed-clock precondition acceptance also passes 19/19 through the pinned PM runner. Combined evidence: linked fence/adoption80, Azure recovery/relation18, focused regression restore23, selected packed7, native matrix19; all executed cases pass. Revert proofs fail23/23 and the late-read mutant fails both decision-binding cases (3/7 including parent). Typecheck, test compilation, docstrings128/128 and changelog check pass. Full coverage/release and final-head bot reviews remain pending in PR92; skipped/unavailable bots are not approval. No rollback, SDK pin bump, history rewrite, live provider call, release or merge. Releasing only this author claim without closing the item."
  "2026-11-06T18:58:34.856Z",codex-astra,"CI fixture correction: the independent peer now retains only PM_ADO_STATEMENT_SOURCES and PM_ADO_STATEMENT_REPORT_DIR among PM_ variables, so its inherited instrumentation hook can load and report counters. Credentials and tracker settings remain filtered. In a disposable copy using Node 22.23.4 and the exact preload generated by scripts/coverage-gate.ts, node --test --test-reporter=spec --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"decision-bound revision guards\" test/history-fence.test.ts passes 23/23 with zero skips. Reverting only the environment-filter correction fails 21/23; two unchecked-dispatch controls still pass. Production guard code is unchanged. Typecheck, test compilation, docstrings (19 files, 128 declarations), and diff checks pass."
